      "message": "gcc 7.5 is one example I have.\n\nFor a minimal test case, e.g. consider the following:\n```c\nint __attribute__((visibility(\"default\"))) some_function(void);\nint  some_function(void) { return 1337; }\nint  more_function(void) { return 0; }\n```\n\nBuilt like this:\n```sh\nx86_64-w64-mingw32-gcc -O3 -Wall -fvisibility\u003dhidden -s src.c -shared -o somelib.dll -Wl,--out-implib,libsomelib.a\nsrc.c: In function \u0027more_function\u0027:\nsrc.c:3:1: warning: visibility attribute not supported in this configuration; ignored\n```\n\n... the build happily exports `more_function` for me with gcc-7.5 with e.g., where it shouldn\u0027t.\n\n\nAs for changing _MSC_VER to _WIN32: That is one thing. But in addition, win32+dllexport checks must come before visibility attributes.\n\nAlso: the autotools side needs the adjustment I made: libtool defines DLL_EXPORT, we need to change that to WEBP_DLL.\n\nAlso: cmake needn\u0027t (shouldn\u0027t) mess with visibility attributes when we are already using dllexport which handles things correctly.",
